# Compose Screen Pattern

```kotlin
@OptIn(ExperimentalMaterial3Api::class)
@Composable
fun {Feature}Screen(
    viewModel: {Feature}ViewModel,
    onNavigateBack: () -> Unit,
    onNavigateTo{Detail}: (String) -> Unit
) {
    val state by viewModel.state.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()
    val snackbarHostState = remember { SnackbarHostState() }

    LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
        viewModel.effect.collect { effect ->
            when (effect) {
                is Effect.NavigateTo{Detail} -> onNavigateTo{Detail}(effect.id)
                is Effect.ShowSnackbar -> snackbarHostState.showSnackbar(effect.message)
            }
        }
    }

    Scaffold(
        snackbarHost = { SnackbarHost(snackbarHostState) },
        topBar = { /* TopAppBar with navigation icon */ }
    ) { paddingValues ->
        when {
            state.isLoading && !state.hasData -> LoadingContent()
            state.error != null && !state.hasData -> ErrorContent(error = state.error!!, onRetry = { ... })
            else -> {Feature}Content(state = state, modifier = Modifier.padding(paddingValues))
        }
    }
}
```

## Rules
- Screen composable receives ViewModel + navigation lambdas (no direct Navigator access)
- Collect `state` via `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()`
- Collect `effect` in `LaunchedEffect(Unit)` — route effects to navigation lambdas
- Loading/Error/Content tri-state pattern using `LoadingContent()` / `ErrorContent()` from ui-components
- Extract content into private sub-composables when screen > 200 lines
- Icons from `painterResource(Res.drawable.ic_xxx)`, strings from `stringResource(Res.string.xxx)`
